.TH MAKE-LABELS 1 "2026-09-30" "label-maker 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
make-labels \- print text and pictures on a sheet of stickers
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print text and pictures on a sheet of stickers.
.br
The default sheet is 110×152 mm, two columns and four rows of
52×34 mm labels.

Text and SVG drawings are vectors.
.br
Photos and other pictures are placed at 300 dpi.
.br
A picture with a flat margin is trimmed to the artwork.

\fB\-\-help\fR prints the short option list.
.br
\fB\-\-man\fR opens this manual.

.SH INSTALL
pipx keeps the tool in its own environment and puts
\fBmake\-labels\fR on your PATH.

From the project folder:

.nf
pipx install .
.fi

While you are changing the code, install it in place so edits
apply immediately:

.nf
pipx install \-\-force \-\-editable .
.fi

After a normal install, pick up later changes with:

.nf
pipx reinstall label\-maker
.fi

Python 3.10 or newer is required.
.br
pipx installs Click and Pillow for you.

You can also run it from this folder without installing.
.br
This creates \fB.venv\fR here:

.nf
python3 \-m venv .venv
\&.venv/bin/pip install \-e .
\&.venv/bin/python make\-labels.py \-\-help
.fi

\fBpython3 make\-labels.py\fR does the same thing when
\fB.venv\fR already exists.
.br
It writes the PDF in the folder you ran it from.

.SH SHEETS
With no arguments the sheet alternates MASTER (green) and SLAVE
(red):

.nf
make\-labels
.fi

That writes \fBlabels.pdf\fR.
.br
\fB\-\-proof\fR adds the alignment grid and a 100 mm ruler.
.br
\fB\-\-outline\fR draws only the grid and the ruler.

.nf
make\-labels \-\-proof \-o check.pdf
make\-labels \-\-outline \-o alignment.pdf
.fi

Other sheets use millimetres.
.br
This is an A4 sheet of 63.5×33.9 mm labels:

.nf
make\-labels \-\-page\-w 210 \-\-page\-h 297 \-\-cols 3 \-\-rows 8 \e
  \-\-lw 63.5 \-\-lh 33.9 \-\-gap\-x 2.5 \-\-gap\-y 0
.fi

\fB\-\-limit 4\fR prints only the first four stickers.
.br
\fB\-\-row 2\fR prints one row.
.br
\fB\-\-skip\-row\fR and \fB\-\-skip\-col\fR leave a row or
column blank.
.br
If the grid does not fit the page, nothing is written unless you
pass \fB\-\-force\fR.

.SH PRINTER CALIBRATION
Printers do not always place a sheet at exactly the expected
origin.
.br
\fB\-\-offset\-x\fR and \fB\-\-offset\-y\fR correct that
mechanical drift without changing the label size or spacing.
.br
A positive \fB\-\-offset\-x\fR moves the grid right.
.br
A positive \fB\-\-offset\-y\fR moves it down.
.br
Negative values move it left or up.

First print a proof on ordinary paper cut to the same dimensions
as the sticker sheet:

.nf
make\-labels \-\-proof \-\-out calibration.pdf
.fi

Place the print behind a sticker sheet and hold both against a
light to compare the proof boxes with the stickers.
.br
Two stickers carry a millimetre scale.
.br
On a sheet of four or more rows they are the second row and the
second-to-last row, at opposite ends.
.br
The first and last rows stay plain, because many printers cannot
print the edge of the page.
.br
On a shorter sheet the ticks sit on the side of the sticker that
faces the middle of the page.
.br
The shortest ticks mark half a millimetre.
.br
The longer ticks are numbered in millimetres.
.br
Read the number at the sticker edge.
.br
That number is the offset.
.br
If the boxes are 2 mm too far left and 1 mm too high, move them
right and down:

.nf
make\-labels \-\-proof \-\-offset\-x 2 \-\-offset\-y 1 \-\-out calibration.pdf
.fi

Print the adjusted proof and check it again.
.br
You can print the second test on the other side of the same
ordinary sheet.
.br
Keep the paper orientation and feed direction the same for every
test.

Use sticker sheets only when the printer supports their
dimensions, material, and media type.
.br
Follow the printer and sticker-sheet instructions for the
correct tray, printable side, and laser or inkjet compatibility.

.SH PRINT SETTINGS
The PDF page has the exact dimensions passed with
\fB\-\-page\-w\fR and \fB\-\-page\-h\fR.
.br
Create or select a paper size in the printer settings with those
same dimensions.
.br
For the default sheet, use 110×152 mm.
.br
Choose the orientation that matches the PDF.

Print at Actual Size or 100%.
.br
Turn off Fit, Shrink oversized pages, Scale to fit, and any
automatic enlargement.
.br
Do not use borderless printing unless the printer can keep it at
100%, because many borderless modes enlarge and crop the page.

Select the tray and media type recommended for the sticker
sheet.
.br
Labels, Heavy Paper, or Cardstock settings may change the feed
speed and temperature.
.br
Turn off duplex printing and print only on the printable side of
the sticker sheet.

Print a proof on ordinary paper before using a sticker sheet.
.br
Measure the printed 100 mm ruler with a physical ruler.
.br
If it is not exactly 100 mm, correct the printer scaling before
changing either offset.
.br
Offsets fix position, not size.

Save the working paper size and printer options as a printer
preset when the print dialog supports presets.
.br
Use the same preset, tray, orientation, and feed direction for
the calibration proof and the sticker sheet.

.SH TEXT
Repeat \fB\-\-text\fR once per sticker.
.br
A real newline or the two characters \fB\en\fR starts another
line.
.br
Colors follow the text stickers in order.
.br
Names (\fBgreen\fR, \fBred\fR, \fBblue\fR, and the others listed
under \fB\-\-color\fR) and \fB#rrggbb\fR both work.
.br
Hebrew uses an embedded font.

.nf
make\-labels \-\-text 'MASTER\enSAW' \-\-text 'SLAVE\enVAC' \-\-color green \-\-color red
make\-labels \-\-text 'מסור\enשואב' \-\-color blue
.fi

\fB\-\-rotate\fR turns the content from the bottom of the
sticker toward the top.
.br
\fB\-\-font\-mm 8\fR sets the letter height.

.SH PICTURES
SVG files are drawn as vectors.
.br
PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, TIFF, and AVIF are embedded at 300
dpi for the sticker.

.nf
make\-labels \-\-image logo.svg \-\-image mark.png
.fi

\fB\-\-trace\fR outlines a flat logo as vector paths.
.br
A photograph stays embedded, because tracing it would not stay
sharp.

One sticker can hold a logo and text.
.br
\fB\-\-combo\fR uses the same sticker text as \fB\-\-cell\fR,
without the row and column.
.br
\fBPATH|TEXT\fR puts the logo before the words.
.br
\fBPATH TEXT\fR as two words means the same thing.
.br
A third field of \fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, or \fBtop\fR is the
layout.
.br
Any other third field is a logo after the words.
.br
A fourth field is the layout.
.br
A colour name or \fB#rrggbb\fR after the last comma colours the
words.
.br
\fB\-\-layout\fR is the default when that text does not name a
layout.
.br
One \fB\-\-layout top\fR puts the logo above the words on every
such combo.
.br
A combo that names an end logo keeps a logo on both sides.
.br
Both logos match the text height and share its vertical center.

\fB\-\-layout left\fR puts the logo before the text.
.br
\fB\-\-layout right\fR puts it after the text.
.br
\fB\-\-layout top\fR puts it above the text.

.nf
make\-labels \-\-combo logo.svg 'MASTER\enSAW'
make\-labels \-\-combo 'logo.svg|SLAVE\enVAC' \-\-layout right \-\-color red
make\-labels \-\-combo 'logo.svg|MASTER|mark.png'
make\-labels \-\-combo 'logo.svg|FIRST|top' \-\-combo 'mark.png|SECOND|right'
.fi

.SH SINGLE CELLS
\fB\-\-cell\fR fills one sticker and leaves the rest of the
sheet blank.
.br
Rows and columns start at 1.
.br
\fB@path\fR is a picture.
.br
\fB@path|text\fR is a logo before the text.
.br
\fB@path|text|end\fR puts a logo on each side.
.br
\fB@|text|end\fR puts the logo after the text.
.br
\fB@path|text|top\fR puts that logo above the words.
.br
\fB@path|text|end|right\fR sets the end logo and the layout.
.br
\fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, and \fBtop\fR in that position are
layouts.
.br
A color after the last comma applies to the text.

.nf
make\-labels \-\-cell '1,1,@logo.svg|מסור,blue'
make\-labels \-\-cell 1,1,@logo.png \-\-cell 1,2,N,black
.fi

.SH SWITCHES
Sizes are millimetres.
.br
Pass a repeatable switch again for another sticker.

.TP
\fB\-W\fR, \fB\-\-page\-w\fR
Default: 110.
.br
Width of the paper.
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-page\-h\fR
Default: 152.
.br
Height of the paper.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-cols\fR
Default: 2.
.br
How many stickers fit across the page.
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-rows\fR
Default: 4.
.br
How many stickers fit down the page.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-lw\fR
Default: 52.
.br
Width of one sticker.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-lh\fR
Default: 34.
.br
Height of one sticker.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gap\-x\fR
Default: 2.7.
.br
Horizontal space between stickers.
.br
When you leave \fB\-\-margin\-x\fR out, the leftover space is
split into equal left and right margins.
.TP
\fB\-G\fR, \fB\-\-gap\-y\fR
Default: 4.
.br
Vertical space between stickers.
.br
When you leave \fB\-\-margin\-y\fR out, the leftover space is
split into equal top and bottom margins.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-margin\-x\fR
Default: centered.
.br
Left margin.
.br
The row of stickers sits in the middle of the page.
.TP
\fB\-M\fR, \fB\-\-margin\-y\fR
Default: centered.
.br
Top margin.
.br
The column of stickers sits in the middle of the page.
.br
\fB\-\-offset\-y\fR is applied after that.
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-offset\-x\fR
Default: 0.
.br
Extra shift to the right, after the margin.
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-offset\-y\fR
Default: 0.
.br
Extra shift down, after the margin.
.br
A positive number moves the stickers down.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-text\fR
Default: MASTER, SLAVE.
.br
Words for one sticker.
.br
Repeat it for the next sticker.
.br
A real line break, or the two characters \fBn\fR, starts a new
line.
.br
With no stickers chosen, the sheet alternates those two words,
green then red.
.TP
\fB\-I\fR, \fB\-\-image\fR
A picture for one sticker.
.br
Repeat it for the next sticker.
.br
SVG is drawn as vectors.
.br
PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, BMP, TIFF, and AVIF are placed at 300 dpi.
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR
Default: off.
.br
Outline a flat logo as vector paths.
.br
A photograph stays an embedded picture, because a trace of it
would not stay sharp.
.TP
\fB\-\-combo\fR \fISPEC\fR
One sticker with a logo and words, using the same text as
\fB\-\-cell\fR.
.br
\fBPATH|TEXT\fR puts the logo before the words.
.br
\fBPATH TEXT\fR as two words means the same thing.
.br
A third field of \fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, or \fBtop\fR is the
layout.
.br
Any other third field is a logo after the words.
.br
A fourth field is the layout.
.br
A colour after the last comma colours the words.
.br
Repeat it for another sticker.
.TP
\fB\-\-layout\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Default: \fBleft\fR.
.br
Default layout for every \fB\-\-combo\fR and \fB\-\-cell\fR that
does not name its own.
.br
\fBtop\fR puts that logo above its words.
.br
\fBleft\fR puts that logo before its words.
.br
\fBright\fR puts that logo after its words.
.br
A sticker that names an end logo keeps a logo on both sides.
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-color\fR
Default: green, red, blue, purple.
.br
Colour of the next text or combo sticker, in order.
.br
Repeat it for the next one.
.br
A picture-only sticker does not take a colour.
.br
A \fB\-\-combo\fR that names its own colour keeps the next
\fB\-\-color\fR for the next sticker.
.br
Use a name or \fB#rrggbb\fR.
.br
Names: black, white, red, green, blue, yellow, orange, purple,
grey, gray, brown.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-cell\fR
Fill one sticker and leave the rest of the sheet blank.
.br
Repeat it for another sticker.
.br
The form is \fBROW,COL,TEXT\fR.
.br
Rows and columns start at 1.
.br
\fB@path\fR is a picture.
.br
\fB@path|text\fR is a logo before the words.
.br
\fB@path|text|end\fR puts a logo on each side.
.br
\fB@|text|end\fR puts the logo after the text.
.br
\fB@path|text|top\fR puts that logo above the words.
.br
\fB@path|text|end|right\fR sets the end logo and the layout.
.br
\fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, and \fBtop\fR in that position are
layouts.
.br
A colour name or \fB#rrggbb\fR after the last comma colours the
words.
.TP
\fB\-F\fR, \fB\-\-font\-mm\fR
Default: fit.
.br
Letter height.
.br
The letters grow until they fit the sticker.
.TP
\fB\-R\fR, \fB\-\-rotate\fR
Default: off.
.br
Turn the sticker contents so they read from the bottom toward
the top.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR
Default: all.
.br
How many stickers to print, starting at the first.
.br
The rest of the grid stays blank.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-row\fR
Default: all.
.br
Which row to print.
.br
Rows start at 1.
.br
The other rows stay blank.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-row\fR
Leave this row blank.
.br
Rows start at 1.
.br
Repeat it for another row.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-col\fR
Leave this column blank.
.br
Columns start at 1.
.br
Repeat it for another column.
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-outline\fR
Default: off.
.br
Draw the sticker borders and a 100 mm ruler, with no words or
pictures.
.br
The file is \fBalignment.pdf\fR when you leave \fB\-\-out\fR
out.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-proof\fR
Default: off.
.br
Draw the words and pictures, and also the borders and the 100 mm
ruler.
.br
The file is \fBproof.pdf\fR when you leave \fB\-\-out\fR out.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Default: off.
.br
Write the PDF even when the stickers run off the page.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR
Default: \fBlabels.pdf\fR.
.br
Where to write the PDF.
.br
\fB\-\-proof\fR writes \fBproof.pdf\fR and \fB\-\-outline\fR
writes \fBalignment.pdf\fR when this switch is left out.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print the short option list and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-man\fR
Open this manual and exit.
.br
When the output is a pipe, the manual is the raw man page
instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-completion\fR \fISHELL\fR
Print a shell completion script and exit.
.br
\fBSHELL\fR is \fBzsh\fR, \fBbash\fR, or \fBfish\fR.

