.SH SHELL COMPLETION
The completion script comes from Click.
.br
It completes switch names, \fB\-\-layout\fR values, colour
names, and file paths for pictures.

For the current terminal:

.nf
eval "$(make\-labels \-\-completion zsh)"
.fi

To keep it in zsh, save the script where \fBcompinit\fR looks:

.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.zfunc
make\-labels \-\-completion zsh > ~/.zfunc/_make\-labels
.fi

Add this to \fB~/.zshrc\fR if tab does nothing, then open a new
terminal:

.nf
fpath=(~/.zfunc $fpath)
autoload \-Uz compinit && compinit
.fi

Bash:

.nf
make\-labels \-\-completion bash > ~/.make\-labels\-complete.bash
.fi

Add this line to \fB~/.bashrc\fR, then open a new terminal:

.nf
source ~/.make\-labels\-complete.bash
.fi

Fish:

.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.config/fish/completions
make\-labels \-\-completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/make\-labels.fish
.fi

.SH FROM PYTHON
\fBrender_pdf\fR returns the PDF bytes.
.br
A future UI can call the same function.

.nf
from labels import SheetSpec, TextSticker, render_pdf

pdf = render_pdf(SheetSpec(
    stickers=(
        TextSticker("MASTER\enSAW", (0.00, 0.55, 0.22)),
        TextSticker("SLAVE\enVAC", (0.82, 0.08, 0.10)),
    ),
))
.fi

A plain dict with the old names (\fBpage_w\fR, \fBcols\fR,
\fBlw\fR, \fBtext\fR, \fBcolor\fR, \fBcell\fR) still works.

